{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nEvery VOTER_ERROR incident is counted twice by the host observability probe, doubling rebar/host:voter_errors. Journald evidence (Gerrit host, 2026-08-22): all five VOTER_ERROR records over Aug 20-22 appear twice with IDENTICAL microsecond timestamps; CloudWatch hourly sums show 2-3 per single-incident hour where journald shows one real error. The metric is useless for rate analysis and will mis-calibrate the companion alarm-recalibration task (ea5d-4932-8554-4544 depends on this fix).\n\nRoot cause (confirmed per rebar-debug; full RCA in the ticket comment): `_voter_error` (src/rebar/review_bot/voter.py) emits the line-start marker `VOTER_ERROR {json}` on TWO paths — `logger.error(line)` and `print(line, file=sys.stderr)`. `configure_logging()` (config.py, wired at import since commit b0ac2544720 / ticket c130-6a87-531e-4441) attaches a stdout StreamHandler with `%(message)s` format, so the logged copy also lands at line start; journald merges the container's stdout and stderr, so the probe's anchored count (infra/scripts/observability.sh:166, `grep -cE '^VOTER_ERROR \\{'`) counts each real error twice. Runtime proof: configured logging → 2 anchor-matching lines per error; unconfigured → 1 (the print; `lastResort` never fires because src/rebar/__init__.py installs a NullHandler on the `rebar` logger).\n\nSibling sweep confirmed the same construct (line-start marker string passed to BOTH a logger call and a stderr print) at four more sites: one live-doubling today (MERGE_CHANGE_ERROR is anchored-counted at observability.sh:196), three latent (RECONCILE_DEGRADED, ARTIFACT_EMIT_ERROR, and LLM_TOKEN_USAGE in voter.py `_emit_token_usage` — logger.info + print, flagged by plan review; no anchored consumer today, doubling is latent for any future host-probe parse). AUTODEPLOY_* markers (autodeploy.sh `marker()`) print once to stderr with no logger path — clean. Downstream-consumer sweep for the logged token-prefixed copy: a repo-wide grep over infra/**, *.tf, *.sh, *.py, *.md finds the tokens consumed ONLY by observability.sh's anchored journald greps (plus prose mentions in .tf/.sh comments); no dashboard, log-shipping filter, or alternate anchor matches the logger-stream copy. The canonical stderr marker line is unchanged by this fix, and the logger copy retains the token as the JSON `event` value, so ad-hoc journal greps for the bare token still hit it.\n\n## Approach\n\nEmitter-side single emission, per the ticket's preferred candidate shape: keep the unconditional `print(line, file=sys.stderr)` as the ONLY line-start marker emission — it is the documented fail-safe and produces exactly one countable line whether logging is configured or not — and change the logger copy at each site to log the structured record body `json.dumps(record, default=str)` WITHOUT the token prefix (the same shape voter's `_emit` already logs for non-marker events). The log-stream copy remains visible to operators and caplog but can never match the probe anchor `^TOKEN \\{`. No probe change needed: observability.sh's documented emitter contract (\"voter.py prints \\\"VOTER_ERROR \\\" + json.dumps(record) to stderr\") stays true; add a one-line note at the anchor comment that the logger copy deliberately does not match. A structural class-guard test prevents a future marker from reintroducing the dual line-start construct.\n\nDefault assumed: RECONCILE_DEGRADED and ARTIFACT_EMIT_ERROR are fixed in scope (same class, same one-line fix) rather than ticketed out — they cite/mirror voter's convention and the fix is identical.\n\n## Scope\n\n- src/rebar/review_bot/voter.py — `_voter_error`: logger.error logs the record body, not the token-prefixed line; comment updated to state the single-line-start-emission contract. Same change in `_emit_token_usage` (logger.info copy of LLM_TOKEN_USAGE).\n- src/rebar/review_bot/voter_merge.py — `merge_change_error`: same change (live-doubling sibling, anchored at observability.sh:196).\n- src/rebar/review_bot/reconcile.py — `_degraded`: same change (latent sibling).\n- src/rebar/review_bot/artifact_emit.py — `_artifact_emit_error`: same change (latent sibling).\n- infra/scripts/observability.sh — comment-only: note at the VOTER_ERROR/MERGE_CHANGE_ERROR anchor blocks that the emitters' logger copy intentionally does not match the anchor (keeps probe and emitter documented in lockstep).\n- tests/unit/test_marker_single_emission_f829.py — new RED-first oracle: subprocess-driven, per emitter × {configured, unconfigured} logging, asserting exactly ONE `^TOKEN \\{` line across stdout+stderr (the journald view); plus the structural class guard scanning src/rebar for the dual-emission construct.\n\n## Testing\n\n- RED before fix: the new test fails on the configured-logging cases (2 anchored lines) for all four emitters; unconfigured cases pass (fallback already single).\n- GREEN after fix: all cases emit exactly one anchored line; unconfigured fallback still one (the print).\n- Regression guard: existing suites (tests/unit/test_review_bot.py incl. the capsys VOTER_ERROR assertion, tests/scripts/test_observability_*.py) still pass — `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_review_bot.py tests/unit/test_marker_single_emission_f829.py tests/scripts -q` plus `make lint`, `make typecheck`, `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check`.\n- Structural guard: the class-guard test fails if any src/rebar file passes a `\"<TOKEN> \" + json.dumps(...)` string to a logger call (the exact construct that doubled).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] Root cause confirmed per rebar-debug (runtime proof: drive _voter_error with configured logging and count journald-shaped lines on stderr+stdout) — RCA comment on this ticket cites the experiment and its counts.\n- [x] One real error produces exactly one probe-countable marker line, while the misconfigured-logging fallback still produces one — verified by the new subprocess test in both logging modes for VOTER_ERROR.\n- [x] Sibling voter_merge.py `merge_change_error` (MERGE_CHANGE_ERROR) single-emits, verified by the same parametrized test.\n- [x] Sibling reconcile.py `_degraded` (RECONCILE_DEGRADED) single-emits, verified by the same parametrized test.\n- [x] Sibling artifact_emit.py `_artifact_emit_error` (ARTIFACT_EMIT_ERROR) single-emits, verified by the same parametrized test.\n- [x] Sibling voter.py `_emit_token_usage` (LLM_TOKEN_USAGE) single-emits, verified by the same parametrized test.\n- [x] Structural class guard: a test scanning src/rebar fails if the dual line-start construct (token-prefixed marker string passed to a logger call) reappears — seen RED against the pre-fix tree, GREEN after.\n- [x] AUTODEPLOY_* audit recorded (clean: single printf-to-stderr path, no logger) — in the RCA comment.\n- [x] [non-codebase] caused_by attributed via the date test (c130-6a87-531e-4441 — the logging-config change activated the second path; the marker's dual emitter predates the transition) and passed as `--caused-by` on the close with `--class=regression`.\n  provenance: environment=rebar tickets tracker (production store); principal=joeoakhart@navapbc.com session agent; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — the caused_by edge is created BY the close command itself (rebar transition ... --class=regression --caused-by=c130-6a87-531e-4441), so it cannot exist in any pre-close snapshot; the attribution evidence (date test) is in the RCA comment on this ticket."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787436885751378001,"uuid":"9391a043-8f1c-4485-b281-95a9d09cdab1"}